    "originalInstructions": "1. For dark part: mix brown sugar, butter, and sour milk\n2. Add flour, raisins, soda dissolved in warm water, molasses, yolks of 3 eggs, cloves, and nutmeg\n3. For white part: mix flour, cornstarch, sweet milk, butter, white sugar, and baking powder\n4. Bake all in four layers\n5. For boiled icing: boil 1 cup white sugar in water enough to dissolve it till it will hair\n6. Beat the white of 1 egg to a stiff froth\n7. Pour the hot sugar on the froth\n8. Flavor to suit the taste and beat till cool enough to stay on the cake\n9. Put layers together with boiled icing",
